---
const signals = [
  {
    date: "24 Aug 2026",
    title: "Acquisition: ADLATUS Robotics",
    summary:
      "NEURA acquired ADLATUS Robotics, adding hundreds of installed autonomous cleaning systems, navigation technology, and application know-how.",
    why:
      "More products and inherited application knowledge may increase the challenge of making technical expertise available across sales and service teams.",
    source:
      "https://neura-robotics.com/de/neura-ubernimmt-adlatus-robotics/",
  },
  {
    date: "13 Aug 2026",
    title: "Acquisition: Bosch Rexroth ACTIVE Shuttle",
    summary:
      "NEURA is integrating Bosch Rexroth's ACTIVE Shuttle into its Physical AI ecosystem.",
    why:
      "Expanding the product portfolio may increase configuration complexity and application-specific questions during the sales process.",
    source:
      "https://neura-robotics.com/de/neura-robotics-ubernimmt-active-shuttle/",
  },
  {
    date: "22 Jul 2026",
    title: "Global Training Expansion",
    summary:
      "NEURA expanded its Physical AI training network with a new NEURA Gym at RWTH Aachen.",
    why:
      "Scaling training suggests that distributing technical knowledge effectively is strategically important.",
    source: "https://neura-robotics.com/de/news/",
  },
  {
    date: "10 Jun 2026",
    title: "Major Growth Financing",
    summary:
      "NEURA announced financing of up to $1.4 billion to accelerate its Physical AI platform.",
    why:
      "Rapid organizational and product scaling can create pressure to scale technical sales knowledge more efficiently.",
    source: "https://neura-robotics.com/news/",
  },
  {
    date: "21 Apr 2026",
    title: "Strategic AWS Partnership",
    summary:
      "NEURA and AWS announced a strategic partnership around the Neuraverse, robotics training, and international market expansion.",
    why:
      "More partners, markets, and deployments can increase the number of people who need access to accurate technical application knowledge.",
    source:
      "https://neura-robotics.com/de/neura-robotics-und-amazon-web-services-starten-strategische-partnerschaft/",
  },
];

const scoreBreakdown = [
  {
    label: "Technical product complexity",
    score: 19,
    max: 20,
    reason: "Robotics, software, integrations, and multiple application environments.",
  },
  {
    label: "Application engineering dependency",
    score: 18,
    max: 20,
    reason: "Robotics deployments typically require application-specific technical expertise.",
  },
  {
    label: "International / partner sales",
    score: 17,
    max: 20,
    reason: "NEURA is expanding through partnerships, ecosystems, and international activity.",
  },
  {
    label: "Growth and change signals",
    score: 18,
    max: 20,
    reason: "Recent acquisitions, financing, partnerships, and training expansion.",
  },
  {
    label: "Evidence of current pain",
    score: 9,
    max: 20,
    reason:
      "There are strong structural indicators, but no direct public evidence confirming an application-engineering bottleneck.",
  },
];

const totalScore = scoreBreakdown.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.score, 0);
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta
      name="viewport"
      content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"
    />

    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A GTM experiment exploring whether public signals can identify potential Bardin opportunities in the German industrial market."
    />

    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />

    <title>Bardin × Germany — NEURA Robotics GTM Experiment</title>

    <style>
      :root {
        --bg: #f6f7f9;
        --card: #ffffff;
        --text: #15171a;
        --muted: #626872;
        --border: #dde1e7;
        --accent: #2d5cff;
        --accent-soft: #edf1ff;
        --success: #17734a;
        --warning: #a86b00;
      }

      * {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        font-family:
          Inter,
          ui-sans-serif,
          system-ui,
          -apple-system,
          BlinkMacSystemFont,
          "Segoe UI",
          sans-serif;
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--text);
        line-height: 1.55;
      }

      a {
        color: inherit;
      }

      main {
        width: min(1100px, calc(100% - 32px));
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 56px 0 80px;
      }

      .hero {
        margin-bottom: 40px;
      }

      .eyebrow {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-bottom: 14px;
        padding: 6px 10px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: var(--accent-soft);
        color: var(--accent);
        font-size: 13px;
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      h1 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
        line-height: 1;
        letter-spacing: -0.04em;
      }

      .subtitle {
        max-width: 720px;
        margin-top: 18px;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 1.1rem;
      }

      .meta-row {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 10px;
        margin-top: 22px;
      }

      .meta-pill {
        padding: 8px 12px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: var(--card);
        font-size: 14px;
      }

      section {
        margin-top: 48px;
      }

      h2 {
        margin-bottom: 18px;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      }

      .grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 16px;
      }

      .card {
        padding: 22px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 18px;
        background: var(--card);
      }

      .snapshot-card strong {
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 5px;
        font-size: 13px;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em;
        color: var(--muted);
      }

      .snapshot-card span {
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      .signal-card {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 12px;
      }

      .signal-date {
        font-size: 13px;
        color: var(--muted);
      }

      .signal-card h3 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 1.15rem;
      }

      .signal-card p {
        margin: 0;
      }

      .why {
        padding: 14px;
        border-radius: 12px;
        background: #f7f8fa;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
      }

      .source-link {
        margin-top: auto;
        padding-top: 4px;
        color: var(--accent);
        font-size: 14px;
        font-weight: 700;
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      .source-link:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
      }

      .score-layout {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 260px 1fr;
        gap: 20px;
        align-items: start;
      }

      .score-box {
        padding: 28px;
        border-radius: 20px;
        background: #15171a;
        color: white;
      }

      .score-number {
        display: block;
        font-size: 4rem;
        line-height: 1;
        font-weight: 800;
        letter-spacing: -0.05em;
      }

      .score-label {
        margin-top: 8px;
        color: #c8ccd2;
      }

      .score-status {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-top: 18px;
        padding: 7px 10px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
        font-size: 13px;
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      .score-items {
        display: grid;
        gap: 12px;
      }

      .score-item {
        padding: 16px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 14px;
        background: var(--card);
      }

      .score-top {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 16px;
        margin-bottom: 5px;
      }

      .score-top strong {
        font-size: 0.98rem;
      }

      .score-value {
        font-weight: 800;
      }

      .score-reason {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.92rem;
      }

      .hypothesis {
        padding: 28px;
        border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
        border-radius: 14px;
        background: var(--card);
        font-size: 1.2rem;
      }

      .hypothesis strong {
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 10px;
        font-size: 13px;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.07em;
        color: var(--accent);
      }

      .question-card {
        padding: 28px;
        border-radius: 18px;
        background: var(--accent-soft);
      }

      .question-card .label {
        margin-bottom: 10px;
        font-size: 13px;
        font-weight: 800;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.06em;
        color: var(--accent);
      }

      .question-card blockquote {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 1.35rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        line-height: 1.4;
      }

      .action-list {
        display: grid;
        gap: 12px;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        list-style: none;
      }

      .action-list li {
        padding: 16px 18px;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 14px;
        background: var(--card);
      }

      footer {
        margin-top: 64px;
        padding-top: 24px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 13px;
      }

      @media (max-width: 760px) {
        main {
          width: min(100% - 22px, 1100px);
          padding-top: 32px;
        }

        .grid,
        .score-layout {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }

        .score-box {
          padding: 22px;
        }

        .score-number {
          font-size: 3.2rem;
        }

        .question-card blockquote {
          font-size: 1.15rem;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <main>
      <header class="hero">
        <span class="eyebrow">Private GTM Experiment</span>

        <h1>Bardin × Germany</h1>

        <p class="subtitle">
          Can publicly available market signals help identify industrial companies
          where technical sales complexity may create a strong opportunity for Bardin?
        </p>

        <div class="meta-row">
          <span class="meta-pill">Pilot account: NEURA Robotics</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Market: Germany / DACH</span>
          <span class="meta-pill">Last reviewed: 27 Aug 2026</span>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section>
        <h2>Account Snapshot</h2>

        <div class="grid">
          <div class="card snapshot-card">
            <strong>Company</strong>
            <span>NEURA Robotics</span>
          </div>

          <div class="card snapshot-card">
            <strong>Location</strong>
            <span>Germany</span>
          </div>

          <div class="card snapshot-card">
            <strong>Industry</strong>
            <span>Robotics / Physical AI</span>
          </div>

          <div class="card snapshot-card">
            <strong>Why relevant</strong>
            <span>
              Complex technical products, rapid expansion, partnerships, and strong
              dependence on application-specific knowledge.
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Recent Signals</h2>

        <div class="grid">
          {
            signals.map((signal) => (
              <article class="card signal-card">
                <span class="signal-date">{signal.date}</span>

                <h3>{signal.title}</h3>

                <p>{signal.summary}</p>

                <div class="why">
                  <strong>Why Bardin may care:</strong><br />
                  {signal.why}
                </div>

                <a
                  class="source-link"
                  href={signal.source}
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                >
                  View source ↗
                </a>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Bardin ICP Fit</h2>

        <div class="score-layout">
          <div class="score-box">
            <span class="score-number">{totalScore}</span>
            <div class="score-label">out of 100</div>
            <span class="score-status">Strong potential fit</span>
          </div>

          <div class="score-items">
            {
              scoreBreakdown.map((item) => (
                <div class="score-item">
                  <div class="score-top">
                    <strong>{item.label}</strong>
                    <span class="score-value">
                      {item.score}/{item.max}
                    </span>
                  </div>

                  <div class="score-reason">{item.reason}</div>
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Pain Hypothesis</h2>

        <div class="hypothesis">
          <strong>Hypothesis — not confirmed fact</strong>

          NEURA's rapid portfolio, ecosystem, and international expansion may make it
          increasingly difficult to distribute application-specific technical knowledge
          across sales, partners, service teams, and newly integrated business units
          without repeatedly involving scarce technical experts.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Best Discovery Question</h2>

        <div class="question-card">
          <div class="label">Suggested question</div>

          <blockquote>
            “When a new customer or partner needs to configure a robot for a specific
            application, how much of that process still depends on getting one of your
            application engineers involved?”
          </blockquote>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Suggested Next Actions</h2>

        <ul class="action-list">
          <li>
            <strong>1. Identify the likely buyer</strong><br />
            Head of Application Engineering, Sales Engineering, Technical Sales, or
            Partner Enablement.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>2. Validate the bottleneck</strong><br />
            Determine whether repetitive technical questions are slowing sales or
            consuming application-engineering capacity.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>3. Understand where knowledge lives</strong><br />
            Ask whether answers currently depend on individual experts, documents,
            internal tools, or informal conversations.
          </li>

          <li>
            <strong>4. Test one Bardin use case</strong><br />
            Select one product family or application area where sales repeatedly needs
            engineering support and test whether that knowledge can be made reusable.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <footer>
        AI-assisted research · Human reviewed · Public sources linked ·
        Hypotheses are intended for validation, not presented as confirmed customer pain.
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
